// ============================================================================
// langMap — file extension and filename to Shiki language id.
//
// GENERATED from GitHub Linguist's `lib/linguist/languages.yml` (linguist main)
// and filtered to the ids this client can highlight: the Shiki web bundle plus
// the extra grammars registered in `shiki.ts`. Do not hand-edit.
//
// Two decisions are baked in, both because Linguist is not a highlighter lookup:
// Shiki ids are not Linguist names (`C++` is `cpp`, `Shell` is `shellscript`),
// and an extension shared by several languages (RenderScript and Rust both use
// `.rs`) is claimed by the first id in the generator's priority list —
// mainstream languages before XML-ish variants. `.h` is forced to C++: its
// grammar parses C, and C++ headers dominate. Anything unsupported is absent, so
// an unknown path degrades to plain text rather than a wrong grammar.
// ============================================================================

